WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.767
As the nation

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:03.803
closes in on the first contest of 2020

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.338
for one of Donald Trump's

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:06.006
most vocal

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:07.440
Republican critics

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.074
is offering

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.010
a very chilling new assessment

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.945
of what his second presidency

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:13.413
would actually look like

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:15.482
if if he's reelected.

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:18.752
Here's CNN's Christine Romans.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.854
A fresh warning from a leading critic

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:22.122
of Donald Trump

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:22.922
about the danger

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.591
posed by the former president

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:26.092
to American democracy.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.761
A vote for Donald Trump

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:29.162
may mean the last election

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.830
that you ever get to vote in.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:31.531
Those comments

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.565
come as Trump attempts

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.934
to turn the tables on such warnings.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.803
Joe Biden is not the defender

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:38.238
of American democracy.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:39.172
The former president,

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:39.773
who is facing

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:41.408
felony charges over his attempts

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:42.776
to overturn the 2020

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:44.077
election, claiming

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:44.778
President Joe

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:47.280
Biden is the real risk to the country.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.916
Joe Biden is the destroyer here

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.484
of American democracy.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.786
It's him and his people.

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:53.720
They're the records

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:54.988
of the American dream.

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:56.022
A spokesman for the Biden

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:56.990
campaign calling

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.591
Trump's comments a, quote,

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.927
desperate attempt at distraction.

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:01.594
Trump's attacks

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:03.129
come as Biden and his allies

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.898
frame the 2024 election

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:05.598
as a choice

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:06.699
between democracy

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.268
and authoritarianism,

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:09.803
signaling how both candidates

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:11.171
are increasingly focused

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:13.606
on a potential general election rematch.

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:14.774
Even as the first votes

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:15.442
in the Republican

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:16.576
nominating contest

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:19.245
won't be cast for another six weeks,

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:22.015
we have to stand up for American values

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:23.483
embedded in the Constitution,

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:25.718
the Declaration of Independence,

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.053
because we know

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:28.922
that Mike Ashley is already proven

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:29.656
they won't

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:30.390
wait to stand up

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:31.825
for our constitutional institutions

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:33.259
and legacy

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.127
because MAGA

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:35.428
statements have made it clear

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:36.830
they're not going to.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.531
In his latest bid for the White House,

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:39.933
Trump has continued to rail

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:41.968
against democratic institutions

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.169
and make false claims

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.004
about the 2020 election.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:45.572
They rigged

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:48.108
the presidential election in 2020,

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:49.843
and we're not going to allow them

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:54.414
to rig the presidential election in 2024.

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:55.882
He also suggested the U.S.

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:57.750
Constitution should be terminated

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.752
in a social media post,

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:00.753
and the former president

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:01.354
has outlined

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:03.256
plans to dramatically reshape

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:04.591
the federal government,

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:05.592
including a pledge

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:07.026
to use the Justice Department

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:08.761
to target political opponents.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:09.662
I mean, if somebody

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:10.964
if I happen to be president

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.632
and I see somebody who's doing well

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:13.366
and beating me

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:14.100
very badly,

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.103
I say go down and indict them.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.239
Mostly that would be

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:21.174
you know, they would be out of business.

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:21.808
They'd be out.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.977
They'd be out of the election.

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.411
Donald Trump has also said that

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:27.147
if reelected to a second term,

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:28.381
that he would make it easier

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:29.816
to fire civil servants

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:31.351
to replace them with a loyalist

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:33.353
as well as he would expand

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:35.288
his hardline immigration policies.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:36.322
And he has called

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.258
for mass deportation now.

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:39.359
This messaging

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:40.660
and this outline of what

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.228
a second term would look like

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.497
is clearly resonating with some people.

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:45.965
We are just about six weeks away

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.700
from the Iowa caucuses

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:48.801
and he is still leading

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.670
all of his Republican rivals

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.039
by a hefty margin in those polls.

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:54.340
And it's not just in Iowa.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.609
He's also leading them nationally as well

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:58.545
Wolf. Kristen Holmes reporting for us.

00:02:58.545 --> 00:03:00.213
Thank you very much. Let's get some more.

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:00.780
All of this.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.782
Joining us now, CNN's Kaitlan Collins,

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.884
a veteran of covering covering the Trump

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:05.351
White House.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.986
Caitlyn, this is not the first time

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:07.820
we've seen Trump

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:10.123
try to turn the tables on his opponents.

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:12.091
But is this a winning idea for him?

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:14.160
Well, it's a tactic that he always uses.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.762
I mean, remember, in the 2016

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:16.563
campaign lit up

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:18.631
after the Access Hollywood tape came out,

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.533
and then at the next debate, he brought

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:21.167
Bill Clinton's

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:22.835
accusers to the pre debate,

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:23.937
had kind of teased this idea

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:25.138
that he might be dropping out

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:25.905
and then brought them.

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.340
He often accuses people

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:28.908
of what they accused him of doing.

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:29.809
And this is the argument

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:31.311
that President Biden has been making long

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:32.979
before he was even in the White House.

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:34.447
He believes it's actually helped.

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:35.815
What helped drive him into

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:37.617
the White House is making this argument

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:38.551
about democracy.

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:39.519
It's what President

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:40.520
Biden plans to use

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.521
as he is trying to seek

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:42.522
a second term here.

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:43.690
And I think when Trump

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.692
is accusing Biden of this, I mean, we can

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:46.893
it's not even based on,

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:47.860
you know, just Trump's words.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:50.163
Look at his actions we all witnessed

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:50.730
as he tried

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:53.733
to overturn the election results in 2020.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:54.801
And it was very clear.

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:55.401
And so

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:56.869
you don't even really have to look deep

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:58.304
into what his advisers are saying

00:03:58.304 --> 00:03:59.072
or his allies.

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.506
You can see it in his own actions

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:02.141
that he was the one who actually tried

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:03.643
to subvert democracy.

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:04.344
But it is something

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:05.478
that they are trying to use.

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:06.279
I mean, they're even going

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:07.247
to the great lengths

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:08.514
of printing out these signs

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:10.016
that say Biden attacks

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:11.651
democracy, pushing it out

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:12.452
because they want to try

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:14.621
to neutralize the argument that they know

00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:15.722
is going to be the chief

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:16.689
one made by President

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:18.391
Biden on the campaign trail.

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:20.193
Can anything really rein in Trump

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:22.362
if there is a second term?

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:23.363
I don't think so.

00:04:23.363 --> 00:04:24.264
I think this is something

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:25.732
that you're hearing from people

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:26.599
who are working with Trump

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:27.100
now, saying

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.134
that it's a positive thing,

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:29.802
that he won't be stymied by people

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:31.337
working against his agenda.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:32.405
But you hear from a lot of people

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:34.307
who worked for him in 2020

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:36.643
or is up to 2020 inside the White House

00:04:36.643 --> 00:04:38.244
who have real concerns about this.

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:39.045
I mean, people like John

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:40.647
Kelly has spoken out about it,

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:41.481
people like Bill Barr,

00:04:41.481 --> 00:04:42.749
the former attorney general.

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:43.683
And they're concerned.

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:44.984
And what you hear from other people

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:45.485
is that

00:04:45.485 --> 00:04:46.419
Trump's not going to hire

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:47.787
anyone who disagrees with him

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:48.588
this time around.

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:49.455
He's only going to hire

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:50.123
people who

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:51.524
not only don't push back on him,

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:53.426
but work to carry out his wishes.

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:54.460
And that was often

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.795
a great frustration of his.

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.196
His first few years in office

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:57.930
was because

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.265
he tried to get something done

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:01.467
and then they would say, that's illegal.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:02.335
It's not doable.

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:03.903
You don't have the authority to do that.

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:05.004
And he would push back.

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:06.139
They're going to be looking to people

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:07.273
who don't do that.

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:08.741
And there's a real concern

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:09.442
that there would impede

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:11.244
the checks and balances on him

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:12.178
if he is reelected,

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:13.579
because he doesn't have to worry

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:14.647
about being reelected again,

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:16.582
which is often something that advisers

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:17.684
would try to use previously

00:05:17.684 --> 00:05:18.318
to try to say, well,

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:19.352
if you do this, it's

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:20.787
going to hurt your reelection.

00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:21.788
And he's not going to have

00:05:21.788 --> 00:05:23.589
the John Kelly's and the bill bars

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.291
and those people working for him.

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:26.559
They've made very clear

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:28.094
that's not who they're going to hire.

00:05:28.094 --> 00:05:28.928
And as Liz Cheney

00:05:28.928 --> 00:05:30.630
warned today, House Republicans

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.765
basically do anything that Trump wants.

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:34.200
That's not going to be an effective check

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.468
either on Capitol Hill.

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:36.302
And he's still way,

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:38.104
way ahead in all the polls.

00:05:38.104 --> 00:05:38.938
See what happens.

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:39.739
All right, Caitlin,

00:05:39.739 --> 00:05:40.973
thank you very, very much.

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:42.475
This important note to our viewers.

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:45.211
We will see Kaitlan later tonight, 9 p.m.

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:47.313
Eastern for the source.

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:49.148
Let's bring in more political experts

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:50.650
right now to break all of this down.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:51.651
And Gloria Borger,

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:53.152
Liz Cheney says the U.S.

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:54.454
is sleepwalking

00:05:54.454 --> 00:05:56.622
into dictatorship, her words.

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:57.790
Is there any reason to think

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.593
Republican voters, though, are listening?

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:01.327
Well, there's one

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:02.695
group of Republican voters

00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:03.696
that are not listening,

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:05.331
and those are the Republican voters

00:06:05.331 --> 00:06:07.133
who are dedicated to Donald Trump

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:08.568
and stick with him

00:06:08.568 --> 00:06:09.969
through thick and thin.

00:06:09.969 --> 00:06:12.038
And the ones who have

00:06:12.038 --> 00:06:13.673
who have gone to him

00:06:13.673 --> 00:06:16.175
since he's been indicted.

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:19.779
But I think there are Republicans

00:06:19.846 --> 00:06:20.613
who are on the

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:23.616
fence who might listen to a Liz Cheney.

00:06:23.616 --> 00:06:25.084
But I think it's incumbent

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:26.786
upon Democrats

00:06:26.786 --> 00:06:27.754
to continue

00:06:27.754 --> 00:06:29.422
to bring the receipts

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:30.390
about the things

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:32.358
that the Donald Trump is saying,

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:33.226
you know, talking

00:06:33.226 --> 00:06:34.961
about using the Justice Department

00:06:34.961 --> 00:06:36.963
for personal retribution,

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:38.698
how he would hollow out the government

00:06:38.698 --> 00:06:42.602
with loyalists, mass deportations.

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:44.971
And I think that those issues

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:46.606
have not been talked about a lot.

00:06:46.606 --> 00:06:47.740
And maybe a lot of people

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:48.608
aren't listening.

00:06:48.608 --> 00:06:50.243
But it's incumbent

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:51.711
upon Democrats to start

00:06:51.711 --> 00:06:53.946
getting the public to focus on

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:55.481
what kind of government

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:56.949
there would be in a second

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:58.551
Donald Trump term

00:06:58.551 --> 00:07:00.420
with advisers

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:02.622
who are loyal to him and no one else.

00:07:02.622 --> 00:07:05.925
And it would be Donald Trump Unchained.

00:07:06.025 --> 00:07:07.960
You know, there would be no guardrails.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:09.095
Yeah, it's amazing

00:07:09.095 --> 00:07:09.962
when you think about it.

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:10.696
Scott Jennings,

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:11.931
let me get your reaction

00:07:11.931 --> 00:07:14.100
to more of what Liz Cheney said

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.735
earlier today in an interview.

00:07:15.735 --> 00:07:17.270
Listen to this.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:18.971
A vote for Donald Trump

00:07:18.971 --> 00:07:20.373
may mean the last election

00:07:20.373 --> 00:07:21.908
that you ever get to vote in.

00:07:21.908 --> 00:07:24.377
And again, I don't say that lightly.

00:07:24.377 --> 00:07:26.245
And I think it's heartbreaking that

00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:27.013
that's where we are.

00:07:27.013 --> 00:07:29.081
But people have to recognize that

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:29.382
a vote

00:07:29.382 --> 00:07:30.082
for Donald Trump

00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:32.752
is a vote against the Constitution.

00:07:32.752 --> 00:07:34.320
So, Scott, how do you respond?

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:35.354
Can you vote for both

00:07:35.354 --> 00:07:39.358
Trump and the Constitution?

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:40.460
Well,

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:43.196
I think that statement is hyperbolic.

00:07:43.196 --> 00:07:45.164
Personally, I guess I have more faith

00:07:45.164 --> 00:07:46.332
in our constitutional order

00:07:46.332 --> 00:07:48.067
and our institutions

00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:49.435
in our other political leaders.

00:07:49.435 --> 00:07:51.370
I know we obviously had a challenge

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.172
to that system in 2020.

00:07:53.172 --> 00:07:53.940
And, you know,

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:55.041
we all saw it unfold

00:07:55.041 --> 00:07:56.576
live on our televisions.

00:07:56.576 --> 00:07:57.910
But the system held

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:00.379
and I actually think the American people

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:01.948
are going to deliver

00:08:01.948 --> 00:08:03.149
a very clear verdict

00:08:03.149 --> 00:08:04.016
in the next election.

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:04.984
I know it's you know,

00:08:04.984 --> 00:08:05.485
we're talking about it's

00:08:05.485 --> 00:08:06.986
going to be close in a handful of states

00:08:06.986 --> 00:08:08.154
and here and there.

00:08:08.154 --> 00:08:09.355
But I think we're going to clearly see

00:08:09.355 --> 00:08:10.957
where the American people want to go.

00:08:10.957 --> 00:08:13.192
I don't know who's going to win, but I.

00:08:13.192 --> 00:08:14.427
I have more faith

00:08:14.427 --> 00:08:15.695
in our constitutional order

00:08:15.695 --> 00:08:17.997
and our institutions than perhaps

00:08:18.064 --> 00:08:19.232
Representative Cheney, who I

00:08:19.232 --> 00:08:20.266
respect greatly is

00:08:20.266 --> 00:08:22.435
is espousing right now.

00:08:22.435 --> 00:08:24.337
Van Jones is with us as well.

00:08:24.337 --> 00:08:27.106
Van, The New York Times writes about this

00:08:27.106 --> 00:08:27.573
and writes

00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:28.875
about what could happen

00:08:28.875 --> 00:08:30.843
in a second Trump administration.

00:08:30.843 --> 00:08:31.477
Let me read to you

00:08:31.477 --> 00:08:33.112
a line from The New York Times.

00:08:33.112 --> 00:08:36.015
Quote, Forces that somewhat contained

00:08:36.015 --> 00:08:37.416
his autocratic tendencies

00:08:37.416 --> 00:08:39.952
in his first term would all be weaker.

00:08:39.952 --> 00:08:41.053
As a result, Mr.

00:08:41.053 --> 00:08:44.056
Trump and his advisers more extreme,

00:08:44.156 --> 00:08:45.591
extreme policy plans

00:08:45.591 --> 00:08:46.759
and ideas for a second

00:08:46.759 --> 00:08:48.794
term would have a greater prospect

00:08:48.794 --> 00:08:50.563
of becoming reality.

00:08:50.563 --> 00:08:51.430
So what worries

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:53.165
you most about a second

00:08:53.165 --> 00:08:55.601
potential Trump term?

00:08:55.601 --> 00:08:55.835
Well,

00:08:55.835 --> 00:08:56.168
the fact that

00:08:56.168 --> 00:08:57.904
he probably be better at it.

00:08:57.904 --> 00:08:59.071
Nobody thought he was going to win.

00:08:59.071 --> 00:09:00.006
He didn't think he was going to win.

00:09:00.006 --> 00:09:01.774
So he had no actual plan.

00:09:01.774 --> 00:09:03.075
He had a campaign team.

00:09:03.075 --> 00:09:04.176
He didn't have a governing team.

00:09:04.176 --> 00:09:05.411
So the whole thing was a dumpster

00:09:05.411 --> 00:09:06.579
fire from the beginning.

00:09:06.579 --> 00:09:08.080
But that was actually a good thing

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:09.448
because a lot of stuff he wanted to do

00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:10.816
he just didn't know how to do.

00:09:10.816 --> 00:09:11.918
Having worked in the White House,

00:09:11.918 --> 00:09:13.219
you spend the first week

00:09:13.219 --> 00:09:14.287
trying to find the restrooms.

00:09:14.287 --> 00:09:16.055
I mean, it's not an easy place

00:09:16.055 --> 00:09:17.823
to learn how to operate.

00:09:17.823 --> 00:09:20.693
So this guy winds up getting a bus.

00:09:20.693 --> 00:09:22.228
You don't know how to drive the bus.

00:09:22.228 --> 00:09:24.030
And so he spends the first four years

00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:25.064
learning how to drive the bus.

00:09:25.064 --> 00:09:25.998
And there were people in there

00:09:25.998 --> 00:09:27.233
who were slowing him down,

00:09:27.233 --> 00:09:29.635
putting up the guardrails this time.

00:09:29.635 --> 00:09:32.004
That won't be the case.

00:09:32.071 --> 00:09:34.473
You got four years to get ready.

00:09:34.473 --> 00:09:36.842
He's got a team of weirdos and wackos

00:09:36.842 --> 00:09:38.411
who thought this thing through.

00:09:38.411 --> 00:09:39.445
And when he gets in there, he's

00:09:39.445 --> 00:09:39.812
going to know

00:09:39.812 --> 00:09:40.913
exactly what he wants to do.

00:09:40.913 --> 00:09:42.381
And now he knows how to drive the bus.

00:09:42.381 --> 00:09:43.883
If you thought he was going fast

00:09:43.883 --> 00:09:44.850
and furious

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:45.785
the first time around,

00:09:45.785 --> 00:09:46.519
you've seen nothing

00:09:46.519 --> 00:09:47.386
on the second time around.

00:09:47.386 --> 00:09:48.220
And it's not just about

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:49.956
you never have another election.

00:09:49.956 --> 00:09:52.091
You thought that last ride was bumpy.

00:09:52.091 --> 00:09:53.492
This is going to be insane.

00:09:53.492 --> 00:09:55.595
And you might have any number of things

00:09:55.595 --> 00:09:56.996
happen to you and your family

00:09:56.996 --> 00:09:58.030
that could have been prevented

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:59.999
by just good orderly governing

00:09:59.999 --> 00:10:00.866
that could happen to you,

00:10:00.866 --> 00:10:01.867
your family, your neighborhood.

00:10:01.867 --> 00:10:02.702
You have no idea

00:10:02.702 --> 00:10:03.836
what you're signing up for.

00:10:03.836 --> 00:10:05.538
You don't like Joe Biden. That's fine.

00:10:05.538 --> 00:10:06.639
But you don't put your family

00:10:06.639 --> 00:10:08.040
on a bus driven by a mad man

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:09.008
because you don't like

00:10:09.008 --> 00:10:10.409
the other bus driver.

00:10:10.409 --> 00:10:11.110
You know, Gloria,

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:13.512
we heard Trump are now accusing Biden

00:10:13.512 --> 00:10:15.247
of being a threat to democracy.

00:10:15.247 --> 00:10:16.882
Should Democrats be concerned

00:10:16.882 --> 00:10:18.351
that Trump can effectively

00:10:18.351 --> 00:10:20.987
turn the tables on Biden?

00:10:20.987 --> 00:10:24.924
Well, Trump does this all the time, Wolf.

00:10:24.991 --> 00:10:27.393
He accuses people of doing things

00:10:27.393 --> 00:10:28.561
that he's accused of.

00:10:28.561 --> 00:10:30.029
And I remember back in

00:10:30.029 --> 00:10:33.432
2016 when he was debating Hillary Clinton

00:10:33.499 --> 00:10:36.335
and she accused him of being a puppet

00:10:36.335 --> 00:10:37.269
of Putin.

00:10:37.269 --> 00:10:39.205
And he said, no, you're the puppet.

00:10:39.205 --> 00:10:41.040
And that's what that's what this is.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:42.274
I think, look, Democrats

00:10:42.274 --> 00:10:43.609
have to counter it.

00:10:43.609 --> 00:10:46.045
They have to counter every charge

00:10:46.045 --> 00:10:47.680
that Donald Trump is making,

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:49.582
no matter how ridiculous.

00:10:49.582 --> 00:10:51.717
And I think this will be

00:10:51.717 --> 00:10:53.019
one of the easier ones

00:10:53.019 --> 00:10:54.120
for them to counter

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:55.254
by reminding people

00:10:55.254 --> 00:10:57.156
that he tried to overturn

00:10:57.156 --> 00:10:58.290
a fair election.

